{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "04QQ", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-germs}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7cce884168b09a22dd17fe23d3797a25816b5783695d86d600f229b2f2bf08c9", "source_text": "Germs of schemes", "source_text_hash": "sha256:601faf040ad319123dd3bb1eb8d82ad5d871abdda741c8b82f793ac0156b439f", "unit_id": "tag:04QQ:title"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04QQ", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(X, x)$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$x$", "MATH_0006": "$f : (X, x) \\to (S, s)$", "MATH_0007": "$f : U \\to S$", "MATH_0008": "$f(x) = s$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0010": "$x$", "MATH_0011": "$f$", "MATH_0012": "$f'$", "MATH_0013": "$f$", "MATH_0014": "$f'$", "MATH_0015": "$x$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-germs}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:561b5adf04d64af53b3fb3186474eb8af1f52328b6d80b75dbeaee41012c2eda", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:fa607683c5d3e4ecfb6b4e81c0754d2190d4eaa4375786b38627091c72f3c03d", "source_text": "Germs of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> A pair <MATH_0001> consisting of a scheme <MATH_0002> and a point <MATH_0003> is\ncalled the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>germ of <MATH_0004> at <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0003> A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism of germs<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> <MATH_0006>\nis an equivalence class of morphisms of schemes <MATH_0007> with <MATH_0008>\nwhere <MATH_0009> is an open neighbourhood of <MATH_0010>. Two such\n<MATH_0011>, <MATH_0012> are said to be equivalent if and only if <MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014>\nagree in some open neighbourhood of <MATH_0015>.\n<STRUCT_0004> We define the <TEXTITOPEN_0003>composition of morphisms of germs<TEXTITCLOSE_0003>\nby composing representatives (this is well defined).\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:40b97c845ee32b20e531d8ec1a604d4e8db058ab40495da70286bf6b38005ec1", "unit_id": "tag:04QR:statement"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04QQ", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:823ef4efd34d96989a01786d67a617cb97c62530048ed20f2d5adac25b86c0da", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nBefore we continue we need one more definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2f770ff1b6d48b0dd4b848374a54a55dc2c3151fd7db24719a4b9147b272ccd0", "unit_id": "tag:04QQ:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "descent", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04QQ", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$f : (X, x) \\to (S, s)$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$f : U \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-etale-morphism-germs}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d9eacfb0a28c2f284fff8d66a15b99fa51e11ce514056d826d953314feb0d5fc", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a7ca52e595712a3a6e3767c43581ae068db9ed1bd4d76be9fff6b752987d7b49", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of germs.\nWe say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001>tale<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> (resp.<SPACE_0001><TEXTITOPEN_0002>smooth<TEXTITCLOSE_0002>) if there exists a\nrepresentative <MATH_0003> of <MATH_0004> which is an <ACCENT_0002>tale morphism\n(resp.<SPACE_0002>a smooth morphism) of schemes.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7bce7ae67e149426df0297bdf4bf619b6eab86ca7a9141b9b9cef5023439e144", "unit_id": "tag:04QS:statement"}
